  "prompt": "Which expression is equivalent to $15x^{7}y^{4}-25x^{5}y^{4}$?",
  "choices": {
    "A": "$15x^{5}y^{4}(x^{2}-5)$",
    "B": "$5x^{5}y^{4}(3x-5)$",
    "C": "$5x^{5}y^{4}(3x^{2}-5)$",
    "D": "$5x^{5}y^{4}(3x^{2}y-5)$"
  },
  "correctAnswer": "C",
  "explanation": "The greatest common factor of $15x^{7}y^{4}$ and $-25x^{5}y^{4}$ is $5x^{5}y^{4}$. Factoring this out: $\\frac{15x^{7}y^{4}}{5x^{5}y^{4}} = 3x^{2}$ and $\\frac{-25x^{5}y^{4}}{5x^{5}y^{4}} = -5$. Therefore, $15x^{7}y^{4}-25x^{5}y^{4} = 5x^{5}y^{4}(3x^{2}-5)$.",
